-- Q1. What is a trigger in PL/SQL?
-- Ans: Trigger ek stored PL/SQL block hai jo
-- specified database event par automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q2. What is the purpose of SALARY_AUDIT?
-- Ans: Ye table salary mein hone wale changes ka
-- record store karti hai.

-- Q3. What does AFTER UPDATE mean?
-- Ans: UPDATE operation ke baad trigger execute hota hai.

-- Q4. What is UPDATE OF BASICSAL?
-- Ans: Iska matlab trigger tab fire hota hai jab
-- BASICSAL column ko UPDATE statement mein specify kiya jata hai.

-- Q5. What is :OLD.BASICSAL?
-- Ans: Ye employee ki update se pehle wali salary batata hai.

-- Q6. What is :NEW.BASICSAL?
-- Ans: Ye employee ki update ke baad wali salary batata hai.

-- Q7. Why is FOR EACH ROW used?
-- Ans: Isse trigger har affected row ke liye execute hota hai.

-- Q8. What is SYSDATE?
-- Ans: SYSDATE database server ki current date aur time return karta hai.

-- Q9. Does a trigger need to be called manually?
-- Ans: Nahi, specified event hone par trigger automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q10. What is an audit table?
-- Ans: Audit table important database changes ka record maintain karti hai.

-- Q11. What is the difference between :OLD and :NEW?
-- Ans: :OLD purani value deta hai aur :NEW nayi value deta hai.

-- Q12. What is the purpose of COMMIT?
-- Ans: COMMIT transaction ke changes permanently save karta hai.

-- Q13. What happens if UPDATE affects no rows?
-- Ans: Koi row update nahi hoti, isliye row-level trigger execute nahi hota.

-- Q14. What is the difference between BEFORE and AFTER triggers?
-- Ans: BEFORE trigger operation se pehle aur AFTER trigger operation ke baad execute hota hai.

-- Q15. What is the purpose of SHOW ERRORS?
-- Ans: Isse trigger compile karte waqt aayi errors check kar sakte hain.
